  ('4d1afa54-c041-5571-b108-8f2a713faf2d', '71bdef5f-d653-5b96-83f9-6a859866d123', $q0$Ticket limit is off by one$q0$, $q0$buy_tickets rejects a purchase that lands exactly on the limit because the check uses >= instead of >, so nobody can ever hold 5 tickets.$q0$, $q0$raffle.py$q0$, $q0$Try to buy exactly the maximum number of tickets for one person.$q0$),
  ('95c473d3-8fa8-5339-b165-37710453f152', '71bdef5f-d653-5b96-83f9-6a859866d123', $q0$Ticket numbers restart for every buyer$q0$, $q0$Numbers are derived from how many tickets the buyer already owns instead of from the global ticket count, so different people get duplicate ticket numbers.$q0$, $q0$raffle.py$q0$, $q0$Look at the ticket numbers after two different people buy tickets.$q0$),
  ('aa9deec1-f4ba-55b4-9c88-14c560d89a0d', '71bdef5f-d653-5b96-83f9-6a859866d123', $q0$Names are not normalized$q0$, $q0$person_key only strips whitespace, so "Ana" and "ana" (or "Ana  Lee" vs "Ana Lee") are counted as different people and can bypass the per-person limit.$q0$, $q0$raffle.py$q0$, $q0$What if the same person types their name differently on their second purchase?$q0$),
  ('aee6d51c-dd04-51b5-bf8f-b965e7024471', '71bdef5f-d653-5b96-83f9-6a859866d123', $q0$Prize pool rounds the wrong way$q0$, $q0$prize_pool computes the pool as 85% rounded down instead of computing the fee rounded down, so the organizer fee is rounded up and the pool loses a cent.$q0$, $q0$pricing.py$q0$, $q0$Compare the prize pool for a single ticket to what the written rule gives.$q0$),
